# Services and EF Core

## Write results

Use `WriteResult<T>` / `WriteStatus`:

| Status | HTTP |
|---|---|
| Success | 201 create / 200 envelope for update-delete |
| NotFound | 404 |
| Forbidden | 403 (authz / system rules / bad caller) |
| ValidationFailed | 400 (blank fields, unknown RoleId, …) |
| Conflict | 409 (duplicate username, email, or role name; role still has users; right already assigned) |

Include a clear `Message` when useful. Map in the controller via `ApiControllerBase` helpers — do not collapse validation into 403.

## Data rules

- Unique indexes on `Users.UserName`, `Users.Email`, `Roles.Name`, `Rights.Name`.
- Normalize username, email, and role name with **trim only** before save. Check uniqueness in the service and catch MySQL duplicate-key on save (`MySqlErrors`).
- Role names are compared case-insensitively. Creating or renaming to an existing name, including `SuperAdmin`, is 409.
- `Users.RoleId` FK delete behavior is **Restrict**. Role delete checks for users and returns 409; the FK is the backup. `RoleRights` cascade when a role is deleted.
- Prefer `AsNoTracking` for reads; pass `CancellationToken` to EF calls. Page with `PageRequest.Normalize`.
- Name request DTOs `userRequest` / `roleRequest` / `rightsRequest` to distinguish from entities.
- Rights catalog and a role's visible rights are filtered to the caller permission claims. Do not add right create/update/delete APIs unless asked.
- No repository layer.
